    {
      "name": "connections",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ask the user for a mandate",
          "request": {
            "name": "Ask the user for a mandate",
            "description": {
              "content": "The agent's operator asks its user for a mandate with these limits, as an RFC 8628 device authorization: the user opens `verification_uri_complete`, compares `user_code` and approves on Keelson's page with a passkey, lowering any limit. Only a client that linked an operator may ask, and the mandate names that operator. The code expires in 15 minutes and is single use.\n\nAn app acting for a user with a token they granted it (`mandates:request`) asks that user only: the request is theirs from the start, so it carries no number to match. The mandate names the app's own operator, or Keelson's hosted operator when the app has none. Through the hosted operator, every app is capped (`hosted-cap`): one user's open mandates and purchases of the last 180 days with apps whose redirect URIs are not a known host's may not pass `HOSTED_CAP_PER_USER_MINOR`, and with all such apps `HOSTED_CAP_KNOWN_PER_USER_MINOR`; every user's funded exposure may not pass `HOSTED_CAP_TOTAL_MINOR`.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "connections"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"reason\": \"<string>\",\n  \"limits\": {\n    \"perPurchaseMinor\": \"<integer>\",\n    \"totalMinor\": \"<integer>\",\n    \"until\": \"<dateTime>\",\n    \"currency\": \"USD\",\n    \"merchants\": [\n      \"mrc_runfast\"\n    ],\n    \"askAboveMinor\": \"<integer>\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Poll for the user's answer",
          "request": {
            "name": "Poll for the user's answer",
            "description": {
              "content": "RFC 8628 §3.4 polling with `grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code`. Until the user decides: `authorization_pending`, or `slow_down` (and 5 more seconds to wait) when polled faster than `interval`. Then `access_denied`, `expired_token`, or the approved mandate's id, once: the device code is spent by the answer that carries it.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "connections",
                "token"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "(Required) "
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "device_code",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "(Required) "
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Read your request's state",
          "request": {
            "name": "Read your request's state",
            "description": {
              "content": "The state of a request this client made, as often as needed: reading it changes nothing and does not spend the device code. Wait `interval` seconds between reads. An app acting for a user (`mandates:request`) reads only that user's requests.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "connections",
                "requests",
                "{{requestId}}"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mandates",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ask the user to change a mandate",
          "request": {
            "name": "Ask the user to change a mandate",
            "description": {
              "content": "The agent asks its user for different limits, with a one-line note the user reads verbatim. The user may lower what is asked and approves with a passkey; the new mandate then replaces this one, whose hold is released. Nothing changes until the user signs. Poll `GET /v1/connections/requests/{id}` for the answer. An app acting for a user (`mandates:request`) asks only about a mandate that user approved for it.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "mandates",
                "{{mandateId}}",
                "changes"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"note\": \"<string>\",\n  \"limits\": {\n    \"perPurchaseMinor\": \"<integer>\",\n    \"totalMinor\": \"<integer>\",\n    \"until\": \"<dateTime>\",\n    \"askAboveMinor\": \"<integer>\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Check a cart against a mandate",
          "request": {
            "name": "Check a cart against a mandate",
            "description": {
              "content": "A dry run: what a countersign of this cart would find, field by field, from the same policy set the TEE legs run, with nothing signed, reserved or logged. The countersign stays the only decision. An app acting for a user (`purchases:write`) checks only under a mandate that user approved for it.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "mandates",
                "{{mandateId}}",
                "check"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"cart\": {\n    \"merchant\": \"<string>\",\n    \"currency\": \"<string>\",\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\n        \"sku\": \"<string>\",\n        \"category\": \"<string>\",\n        \"qty\": \"<integer>\",\n        \"unit_minor\": \"<integer>\",\n        \"size\": \"<string,null>\",\n        \"color\": \"<string,null>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"return_days\": \"<integer>\",\n    \"returns_free\": \"<boolean>\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "tee",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Countersign a cart",
          "request": {
            "name": "Countersign a cart",
            "description": {
              "content": "Sends the cart to the TEE legs in order and returns the countersignatures only when both agree. A DENY is countersigned too. An app acting for a user (`purchases:write`) countersigns only under a mandate that user approved for it; under a mandate of Keelson's hosted operator it sends `mandateId` and Keelson closes the mandate with that operator's key over the request id and this cart, and nothing else. A cart is bought once per mandate: while a purchase of the same cart is in flight, or for ten minutes after it was captured, another request for it is answered `409 purchase-exists` with that purchase's id, whatever its request id, evidence or `Idempotency-Key`. Retrying after a lost answer is therefore safe; to buy the same cart again on purpose, name that purchase in `repeatOf`.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "countersign"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"cart\": {\n    \"merchant\": \"<string>\",\n    \"currency\": \"<string>\",\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\n        \"sku\": \"<string>\",\n        \"category\": \"<string>\",\n        \"qty\": \"<integer>\",\n        \"unit_minor\": \"<integer>\",\n        \"size\": \"<string,null>\",\n        \"color\": \"<string,null>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"return_days\": \"<integer>\",\n    \"returns_free\": \"<boolean>\"\n  },\n  \"unit\": {},\n  \"evidenceRoot\": \"<string>\",\n  \"authorizationId\": \"<string>\",\n  \"closedMandate\": \"<string>\",\n  \"mandateId\": \"<string>\",\n  \"requestId\": \"<string>\",\n  \"evidence\": {},\n  \"live\": {\n    \"store\": \"<uri>\"\n  },\n  \"repeatOf\": \"<string>\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Attested TEE signers",
          "request": {
            "name": "Attested TEE signers",
            "description": {
              "content": "The signers whose countersignatures are accepted, each with the attestation it was admitted from, and the measurements the deployment publishes. A verifier checks the attestations itself.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tee",
                "attestations"
